{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles","id":608026,"title":"Hunter 2nd Edition- the Slasher Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T09:46:03-07:00","id":608026,"title":"Hunter 2nd Edition- the Slasher Chronicles","content":"It's official, my friends- check the brochure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:52:48-07:00","id":608054,"title":"","content":"Huh. Slasher.<br /> <br /> Would not have been my choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:57:57-07:00","id":608060,"title":"","content":"yeah, mine too- but I can understand that choice. The Chronicles usually focus around something which force the characters out of their comfort zone- something which is usually outside of their preview, takes them by surprise and force rivals and sworn enemies to make alliances against the common threat. Slashers fit that niche pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:01:09-07:00","id":608066,"title":"","content":"True that. And Slashers are some of my favorite antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:09:17-07:00","id":608115,"title":"","content":"You know, the most interesting thing is that the 2nd ed book is presented to be &quot;compatible with other gamelines&quot;. While nothing actually really stops you from doing crossovers now, the common notion is that Hunter works better in its own &quot;mini-world&quot;. I wonder if that would be changed in the next edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T10:19:51-07:00","id":608160,"title":"","content":"I hope so.<br /> <br /> I like that the books present tools and options to make your own monsters and give direction on how to make the other gamelines within the dread power system, as well as the unique subsets of the other games. Hunter should be the first game people buy if for no other reason than that. THAT SAID, I've never really used it myself when I was running Hunter. I always went to the other books, and pitted them against Awakening mages and Lost changelings and Requiem vampires and so on.<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw once said that if you put a group of hunters against an Awakening mage, the deck was incredibly stacked against the hunters(as a broad generality). And there are times where that's right-I have had to fudge some rules to make things happen at times, and I never quite liked how that was the case. Should it be hard for a cell to take on a Mage? Yes, but not so stacked. Should a compact cell be able to take on a pack? Tough, lots of planning to make it work, but yeah. Should conspiracy agents be able to take on a meret just raised? Okay maybe not quite that extreme, but still, the answer is yes-Vigil hunters should be able to go have an impact on the world. If there's a reason the supernatural keep up a Masquerade, it's because <i>hunters are effective</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:03:59-07:00","id":608375,"title":"","content":"I think Dave Brookshaw was talking specifically in terms of the RAW for Mage. Ignoring all the narrative, the difference between a cabal and a cell is that one of them can teleport and read minds, whilst the other can't (generally). Trying to balance that is probably more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:22:39-07:00","id":608385,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel like there's some tension in Hunter with the whole &quot;candle in the darkness/underdog defending the ignorant&quot; vibe and being a major gameline. There's only so much that you can expand on with the concept until it starts getting diluted. I think we kinda saw some of that with the gameline. A lot of the groups weren't even really hunters or that ignorant/underdoggy and that made sense-the supernatural in the WoD is not a purely negative thing. It makes perfect sense that people would take advantage of it after the initial shock...but I do think it kinda diluted the core theme and made for some thematic messiness. <br /> <br /> I've seen some notions around (I think Dataweaver was in favor of it?) of making &quot;Hunter&quot; a blue book mrtal supplement concerned with how humans and minor supernatural humans interact with the supernatural world in general, with hunting being a subset. That sounds pretty cool to me honestly...I can't help but feel that some of the groups would be improved if they didn't have to be focused around &quot;the Vigil&quot;. It'd be interesting to see what the &quot;aware&quot; human world is like without the thematic influence of any one major gameline (and that includes Hunter). <br /> <br /> Seems they're not going that route though which is understandable. A lot of NWOD 2nd Edition work has been great so I'm cautiously optimistic. I do kinda hope they move Slashers away from being so obviously a specific movie villain pastiche though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:26:42-07:00","id":608389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608375#post608375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Dave Brookshaw was talking specifically in terms of the RAW for Mage. Ignoring all the narrative, the difference between a cabal and a cell is that one of them can teleport and read minds, whilst the other can't (generally). Trying to balance that is probably more trouble than it's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the idea of making Hunter compatible with the other gamelines rather than relying simply on the Hunter versions appeal to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I disagree with the notion that hunters are underdogs. Again, there's a reason why the supernatural prefer to play quiet, and yes, threat of the masses is one big reason, but I think the effectiveness of hunters is a bigger reason. It's easy to see the underdog aspect given how they are supposed to be just humans against bigger things, but hunters have to contribute significantly to the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-30-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:32:45-07:00","id":608393,"title":"","content":"Slasher Chronicles?<br /> <br /> On the one hand Slashers are awesome.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, most of them aren't even 'monsters', they're just really nasty humans. (Oddly enough, MachineIV was the one who made me feel this way by crushing my idea for the Cult Chronicles)<br /> <br /> On the gripping hand a 'core' antagonist for Hunter clashes with the diversity of the gameline.<br /> <br /> On the final thoughts - it's not like core antagonists are really that core anyway. So it should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:38:00-07:00","id":608397,"title":"","content":"I honestly would have gone for just &quot;Mad/Infinite Shadows Chronicle&quot;.<br /> <br /> But Slashers do upset the applecart, in quite a number of ways, so I can get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T13:38:03-07:00","id":608398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608385#post608385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel like there's some tension in Hunter with the whole &quot;candle in the darkness/underdog defending the ignorant&quot; vibe and being a major gameline. There's only so much that you can expand on with the concept until it starts getting diluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to dilute that concept. There's 12 organisations (+ Cells) in the core book alone. There's only so many ways to do underdogs, I want to see some top dogs in there too. When T:FV, the MM or AKD go on the warpath I want entire cities of monsters to quake in their boots at the thought of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608385#post608385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen some notions around (I think Dataweaver was in favor of it?) of making &quot;Hunter&quot; a blue book mrtal supplement concerned with how humans and minor supernatural humans interact with the supernatural world in general, with hunting being a subset. That sounds pretty cool to me honestly...I can't help but feel that some of the groups would be improved if they didn't have to be focused around &quot;the Vigil&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's like that already. Look at Null Mysteriis, Network Zero, Talbot Group, even Cherion.<br /> <br /> Though there's lots more room in this direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:57:05-07:00","id":608462,"title":"","content":"I like it. Slashers are monsters in the only way that truly matters: they do monstrous things. More importantly, they're the only antagonists in the whole World of Darkness that are uniquely connected to hunters; so it makes sense to me that they're being given a special place in the second edition. <br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that this is being released concurrently with the second edition of the World of Darkness core rulebook, otherwise known as \u201cthe <i>other</i> book that features mortal protagonists\u201d. And WoD2e is going to feature extensive rules for \u201chow to make monsters\u201d, according to the brochure. It makes me wonder what Hunter 2e is going to do with respect to its antagonists; I would not object to the notion of WoD taking over the workload of providing \u201cgameline approximations\u201d (along with Outsiders that don't fit neatly in any of the existing pigeonholes) while Hunter gets recast as a \u201ccrossover-friendly\u201d game in a manner similar to what <b>Beast</b> is doing \u2014 albeit from a far more contentious angle. That is, let WoD2e focus more heavily on the \u201cunderdogs/ignorants\u201d angle, whereas Hunter2e gets to focus more heavily on mortals who <i>know what they're up against</i>, with Tactics, Endowments, etc. that are designed primarily with Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, etc. in mind rather than generic vampires, werewolves, witches, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:29:10-07:00","id":608508,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To everyone: what do you believe Hunter is about as a major gameline? What is its focus? What makes it cool and interesting and special to you?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608389#post608389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why the idea of making Hunter compatible with the other gamelines rather than relying simply on the Hunter versions appeal to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I disagree with the notion that hunters are underdogs. Again, there's a reason why the supernatural prefer to play quiet, and yes, threat of the masses is one big reason, but I think the effectiveness of hunters is a bigger reason. It's easy to see the underdog aspect given how they are supposed to be just humans against bigger things, but hunters have to contribute significantly to the Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of the &quot;Masquerade&quot; as really a thing in NWOD 2nd Edition. I mean, certainly a vampire doesn't want mortals to find out about him and come after him but that's a very personal thing. I don't see a concentrated effort among &quot;the supernatural&quot; to hide from regular humanity (not least because that's an incredibly diverse group). The semi-ignorance of humanity is much more due to their own innate natures-everybody knows about the supernatural, it's just easier to not acknowledge it (Breaking Points and such).. I'd say the supernatural &quot;playing quiet&quot; is more about convenience than fear.<br /> <br /> I don't even think of the &quot;threat of the masses&quot; as that big a factor either. The supernatural is deeply embedded in the NWOD (and is again, extremely diverse), it's not universally hostile to humanity. In the event that people stopped having Breaking Points towards the supernatural, I think you'd have tons and tons of people joining and aligning themselves with lots of supernatural groups rather than fighting against them-even the less friendly ones. Heck, mortal governments would seem to be natural allies to (for example) the Forsaken against the Pure and other spirits out of simple self-interest.. I mean, there are supernatural things that could reasonably be called gods in the NWOD. People in the real world worshipped the moon and sun. If we knew these had actual incredibly powerful spirits that have agents in our world? I think you'd see a lot Helios/Luna cults in the modern day. <br /> <br /> That's another thing that's I feel is a little weird about Hunter actually. It pushes the notion of &quot;the supernatural&quot; on one side and &quot;humanity&quot; on the other when I don't think that really works in the NWOD. The supernatural is so deeply entertwined with the world...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hm, hope I didn't put my foot in my mouth. I generally agree with a ton of what you say usually.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Anyways, I feel like the 1st Edition gameline pushed the notion of Hunters being underdogs. I'd ask you the question at the top of my post though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608398#post608398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I want to dilute that concept. There's 12 organisations (+ Cells) in the core book alone. There's only so many ways to do underdogs, I want to see some top dogs in there too. When T:FV, the MM or AKD go on the warpath I want entire cities of monsters to quake in their boots at the thought of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's like that already. Look at Null Mysteriis, Network Zero, Talbot Group, even Cherion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Though there's lots more room in this direction.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Well that's kind of what I mean when I say the themes were kind of diluted. Hunter is a major gameline, not a blue book and it has specific themes of its own. I mean, you bring up those other organizations and I agree with you! But the gameline is called <i>Hunter</i>. Not &quot;Filmer&quot; or &quot;Scientist&quot; Now, it's been a while since I read the core book but I very much recall a focus on &quot;the Vigil&quot; and being &quot;a candle in the darkness&quot; and well, hunting monsters. This got kind of strange for me when-for example- I read about the Cheiron Group. I mean what Vigil are they upholding? How the heck are they a &quot;candle in the darkness&quot;? And Null Mysteriis isn't really interested in hunting as much as understanding. <br /> <br /> Hunter is very much akin to Vtr and Mta in being a major gameline that tries to have specific themes, not a blue book that doesn't adhere to an overarching focus. Except that those themes were a bit too narrow and so they had to expand beyond that. So I don't think it's &quot;like that already&quot;. I think it certainly <i>could</i> and that could be awesome...but I don't think it's already their. <br /> <br /> I'd ask the question at the top of my post to you. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:38:27-07:00","id":608517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608508#post608508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To everyone: what do you believe Hunter is about as a major gameline? What is its focus? What makes it cool and interesting and special to you?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> It's a toolbox.<br /> <br /> I don't want it to have a theme. I want each Comapct and Conspiracy to have their own theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T15:56:51-07:00","id":608531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608517#post608517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's a toolbox.<br /> <br /> I don't want it to have a theme. I want each Comapct and Conspiracy to have their own theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I don't think you''ll get your wish. I mean, it's still called Hunter: The Vigil and Slashers are a part of the title... <br /> <br /> (As an aside, how did MachineIV crush your idea for Cult Chronicles?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:35:19-07:00","id":608602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608508#post608508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To everyone: what do you believe Hunter is about as a major gameline? What is its focus? What makes it cool and interesting and special to you?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it's their competence. Even an independent cell with no ties to any Compacts or Conspiracies should have an edge over an equivalent troupe of blue-book protagonists. <i>At a minimum,</i> they benefit from Practical Experience with the supernatural that lets them learn and adapt much more quickly than those who haven\u2019t taken up the Vigil. <br /> <br /> More generally, I see \u201ctaking up the Vigil\u201d as a case of at least partially breaking free of the Sleeping Curse that causes most mortals in the World of Darkness to shy away from the supernatural and to pretend it doesn't exist. Indeed, I\u2019d be OK if every one of the Vigilant had an innate resistance to Breaking Points brought on by witnessing supernatural phenomena, with an option to attain full immunity from them \u2014 not because they are in any way supernatural themselves, but merely because the supernatural doesn't have the same hold on them that it does on others. Being a candle in the dark is a metaphor for their tendency to see the supernatural for what it is and not hide from it. <i>All</i> hunters, from the first-tier individuals who get by just on their wits and home-made arsenals to the third-tier professionals who wield cutting-edge Endowments, should have that edge, as that\u2019s the key thing that sets a hunter apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:52:46-07:00","id":608619,"title":"","content":"Not extremely happy that Slashers seem to be the main antagonist, but it doesn't matter in the long run. I love Hunter. It's my favorite game, and I will buy the **** out of this upon release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:58:41-07:00","id":608621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608508#post608508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's kind of what I mean when I say the themes were kind of diluted. Hunter is a major gameline, not a blue book and it has specific themes of its own. I mean, you bring up those other organizations and I agree with you! But the gameline is called <i>Hunter</i>. Not &quot;Filmer&quot; or &quot;Scientist&quot; Now, it's been a while since I read the core book but I very much recall a focus on &quot;the Vigil&quot; and being &quot;a candle in the darkness&quot; and well, hunting monsters. This got kind of strange for me when-for example- I read about the Cheiron Group. I mean what Vigil are they upholding? How the heck are they a &quot;candle in the darkness&quot;? And Null Mysteriis isn't really interested in hunting as much as understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Hunter 1ED core for a few days now I can certainly say that you do not get &quot;the Vigil&quot;. In Hunters point of view, they <b>are</b> responsible for &quot;the masses&quot;. Or at least <b>profitable</b> by them. They fight, learn or communicate with monsters as much as they can because they know that rest of humanity cannot- it's their job <b>only because</b> they broke the Sleeping Curse and saw how the world really works. They calling it &quot;taking the Vigil&quot; but it's more &quot;being put in deadly situation and you can let it get all the worsen if done nothing&quot;. Hunters try to help the world, because they know that without them, world would be much darker place - maybe even monsters would metaphorically <i>&quot;eat it&quot;</i>. Is it their own delusion? Maybe. But to be a Hunter is to see a world of horror and trying to make it in the world of wonder, at least in small part. Sometimes it's killing the monster and saving the day. Other times is just understanding magical regeneration and trying to make a cure.<br /> <br /> Did you not watched <b><i>Supernatural</i></b> for at least it's first five seasons to get moral ambiguity of it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2015, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:05:33-07:00","id":608624,"title":"","content":"As to Slashers as major antagonists of 2ED - like it was written in the 1ED corebook - they are the dark mirror of Hunters. Hey, most are ex-Hunters themselves! And they are really only unique antagonists of the line - it does have sense to make them central to the game when looking for &quot;special trouble&quot; of new edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:10:42-07:00","id":608730,"title":"","content":"Yeah. They just focus on a different prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:24:38-07:00","id":608738,"title":"","content":"It could be Slashers are the highlighted antagonists, not the main antagonists. In Werewolf the main antagonists are spirits, not idigam specifically. Depending on what they do with WoD 2.0, I would assume Hunter would have a big focus on monsters. The monsters as presented in Hunter don't lend themselves well to a Chronicle. A monster is usually a story antagonist. Game line monsters don't count because that is more of a crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:41:01-07:00","id":608755,"title":"","content":"The Chronicle antagonists seem to be more about being 'out of context' stuff. Idigam seem like spirits but aren't exactly spirits. Strix are like vampires but really unlike them. Both are a puzzle neither are really built to solve. I really like Slashers, it's going to be cool to see them incorporated fully into hunter.<br /> <br /> Now all we need is Something: the Possessed Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T19:15:50-07:00","id":608774,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more equivalence in the Conspiracies, TFV and AKD seemed really cool but their benefits were kind of clunky compared to the MM or Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608160#post608160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave Brookshaw once said that if you put a group of hunters against an Awakening mage, the deck was incredibly stacked against the hunters(as a broad generality). And there are times where that's right-I have had to fudge some rules to make things happen at times, and I never quite liked how that was the case. Should it be hard for a cell to take on a Mage? Yes, but not so stacked. Should a compact cell be able to take on a pack? Tough, lots of planning to make it work, but yeah. Should conspiracy agents be able to take on a meret just raised? Okay maybe not quite that extreme, but still, the answer is yes-Vigil hunters should be able to go have an impact on the world. If there's a reason the supernatural keep up a Masquerade, it's because <i>hunters are effective</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentacle Mages <i>don't</i> want to maintain the masquerade, though, they would much rather everyone be at least a Sleepwalker. They &quot;keep&quot; the masquerade because of the influence of the Abyss and ultimately the Seers: it is not a choice, it is absolute Tyranny.<br /> <br /> Demons keep up their version of the masquerade because they're afraid of the God Machine, not Mortals (who generally don't even have a way to figure out they're Demons).<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters... don't really maintain a masquerade, they just don't cause much of a ruckus as they're mainly focused on cleaning up Underworld related detritus, thereby reinforcing the masquerade by accident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-30-2015, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T20:05:06-07:00","id":608798,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I've always felt that Slashers were the <i>de facto</i> antagonists when pitted against Hunters.<br /> <br /> Granted, Hunters are built from a spectrum of varying backgrounds and some of the iconic, media-based hunters specialize in hunting down one type of supernatural creature (barring <i>Supernatural</i>, for the most part). However, I felt that Slashers at least cover a wide area for the &quot;not-revealed-to-the-seedy-underbelly-of-reality&quot;-type Hunters. It is pretty much assumed that most Hunters have had some sort of contact with a supernatural creature, which led to their holding of the Vigil. However, Slashers aren't really that locked into the realm of arbitrary skepticism. The authorities are going to have an easier time explaining off a series of odd killings involving bite marks around the neck as some sort of serial killer with a peculiar modus operandi. <br /> <br /> If anything, I hope that <i>The Slasher Chronicles</i> focuses on the mundane parts of a Hunter's life. I feel that the Vigil engulfs more of a Hunter's life without having much crunch to it. Like, how is Sally gonna balance family life, college life, a part-time job, and setting a den of Vampires on fire without getting burnt out? <i>[As a side-note, candle and light-themed motifs would be interesting to see, considering the Vigil is essentially a light in the darkness that may flicker and dim with the pain of having to hold it. No, this has nothing to do with me coming up with the &quot;burnt out&quot; idea, how dare you?]</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T20:12:30-07:00","id":608801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608774#post608774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see more equivalence in the Conspiracies, TFV and AKD seemed really cool but their benefits were kind of clunky compared to the MM or Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> Demons keep up their version of the masquerade because they're afraid of the God Machine, not Mortals (who generally don't even have a way to figure out they're Demons).<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters... don't really maintain a masquerade, they just don't cause much of a ruckus as they're mainly focused on cleaning up Underworld related detritus, thereby reinforcing the masquerade by accident.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, Demons have little to fear about Mortals finding out about them. Hell, a few may even go so far as freaking advertise themselves as wheelers and dealers and as the man/woman who can &quot;make things happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are quite correct that's only the GM's attention that they mostly hide from.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters, from my understanding, keep a rough masquerade but it's not anything formal but rather born out of practicality more so than anything else. Having people follow you usually creates Ghosts real quick and that makes your job harder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T21:36:41-07:00","id":608897,"title":"","content":"My point is that in the pie graphs of reasons that make up a sort of consensual agreement on a Masquerade between the splats that is kept to varying degrees(from passive disinterested indulgence to cultural cornerstone), hunters being effective should be in the realm of the three biggest slices of &quot;Why we don't just come out of the shadows and take everything.&quot; I want some delivery on the concept of &quot;We're not about to take on humanity&quot; that is a common trope in this sort of spliel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T23:01:33-07:00","id":608987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608897#post608897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that in the pie graphs of reasons that make up a sort of consensual agreement on a Masquerade between the splats that is kept to varying degrees(from passive disinterested indulgence to cultural cornerstone), hunters being effective should be in the realm of the three biggest slices of &quot;Why we don't just come out of the shadows and take everything.&quot; I want some delivery on the concept of &quot;We're not about to take on humanity&quot; that is a common trope in this sort of spliel.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I guess my point is that &quot;scared/cautious of Hunters/Humanity&quot; only works for some of the lines.<br /> <br /> But I agree in spirit, for those lines it's applicable &quot;don't fuck with the teeming mass of humanity that dominates the planet&quot; should be high up there on the priority list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:50:54-07:00","id":609078,"title":"","content":"Slasher Chronicle.... I do like them as a Dark Mirror.<br /> <br /> Though I'm sad we are not getting the Everything Chronicles :P<br /> <br /> Hopes:<br /> - Hunter was something of a minor template(-ish?) thing in the past, but I'm hoping it will step up a bit as a major template. Alternate Integrity seems like the perfect way to handle the Tells, and a divide between normal life and Vigil seems like a good way to contrast that.<br /> - review every organization, and don't be afraid to make a compact into a conspiracy or vice-versa. The 2 major differences compacts vs conspiracies were: scope and Endowments. Now Compacts are also getting Endowments, so that doesn't matter, and even scope was pretty iffy to be honest, since we had at least a few global compacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T00:55:15-07:00","id":609079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608508#post608508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]To everyone: what do you believe Hunter is about as a major gameline? What is its focus? What makes it cool and interesting and special to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually believe that the &quot;Light into the Shadows&quot; metaphor actually represent quit well what Hunter is. For me, Hunter is about taking a stand- is about taking the candle, and dare to cast light into the deep, deep darkness and see what is hidden there. It is about actively entering the shadows and banishing them away. As MachinelV once said, if the other lines are about asking questions, Hunter is about giving (some of those) answers. Hunter is about people who fight to unknown- it is not about the monsters. The monsters are just a symptom. The real enemy of the hunters is ignorance- both of humans and monsters. Because of that, experienced hunters work well with all kinds of weird shit which the night throws on them, and it makes them taking for granted things which make both mortals and monsters scream with horror. A Kindred meeting one of the Wicked Dead would say &quot;what the hell is that?!&quot;. An hunter would say &quot;cut its head or burn it with fire. One of those always works&quot;. And that before we even start talking about Conspiracies and their Endowments- for so many of their powers and &quot;special tricks&quot; would make the average mage bump her head in the wall while screaming &quot;thing don't work like that!&quot;- only that they do. Tough luck.<br /> <br /> And this is why Slashers makes such a good Chronicle antagonists for Hunter. I mean, look on the other lines- vampire is busy at plotting her next political move to dethrone the local Prince, when a strix comes to town and destroys all of her year long plans. A pack of werewolves chasing down a totem of a rival Pure when something alien and ancient eats that spirit. A mage is in a middle of a long research until she feel something tingling with her &quot;mage senses&quot; and she have to check it out. A lone promethean walks in his Pilgrim toward humanity when suddenly the Divine Fire descends and change the world, giving him both an hope and despair. A changeling is busy at building her new life when suddenly the huntsmen come and threat to take everything from her.<br /> <br /> And what Slashers do?<br /> <br /> Slashers bring darkness into the light- casting deep shadows against the candle. An hunter is working on a new case- something steals human hearts and drain them from blood. One member of the cell says it must be some sort of vampire, for the periods in which the victims are killed are periodical and hearts are connected to life energy. Another says it must be a witch, maybe one which works on a very complicated ceremony he once read about in an old book. A third would claim it is a kind of shapeshifter who can change its human form after doing some kind of a sacred hunt. It could also be a mad cultist, a desperate necromancer, a pact made with the Fae or with Hell, and so on and so on.. That is, until they finally meet the murderer and discover he is just a person. A regular human being- maybe it is even the local gardener or the kid next door, someone who looks perfectly normal with a loving family and good job. He isn't compelled by some supernatural power to kill, she doesn't have a reason. It simply who they are- bad people, very very bad people.<br /> <br /> So if hunter is about answering questions, the Slashers force you to ask those questions again. Are they monsters? Are they humans? What does being a &quot;human&quot; actually means? Could they be fixed? Do they deserve a second chance? What makes a normal person start killing off his own kind? Is it in the blood? A psychological effect? Could your friends turn into that? Could you turn into that? When do you cross the line between a human and something else- and most of all, if humans can become monsters, could monsters become humans?<br /> <br /> In short, Hunter is a game about Light and Shadows, answers and questions. It doesn't matter if you are a lone hunter in the night, if you have the backup of your friends with you or even if you are a child of the devil or a drug kingpin or a semi-cannibalistic monster eater. The only thing that matters is that you take a stand and step into the night, willing to endanger your own soul in order to drive away the darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:23:08-07:00","id":609235,"title":"","content":"To me, Hunter is the original crossover game. Much like Beasts, the game is meant to take all the game lines, and use them as the primary source of plot hooks, except as antagonists instead of friends. Simply put, the point of Hunter is to have a game that focuses on humanity fighting back against the night and everything in it. The game has been called Mortal 2.0, and so it is. That is the appeal - being Buffy and the Scooby gang against the monsters. <br /> <br /> I also find the idea that we need to have watered down versions of the supes to be a bit annoying. The monsters have weaknesses for a reason, after all. While hunters are underdogs, they should make up for it with being clever and using evry advantage they can milk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:29:26-07:00","id":609236,"title":"","content":"Well I'm somewhat disappointed that the Hunter chronicle is going to be so antagonist focus - I was hoping for a more open and nuanced appreciation of the setting, its compacts and conspiracies, and the dark mirror of supernatural society that envelopes the Vigil - much like the up coming Mage chronicle.<br /> <br /> Now don't get me wrong, I like slashers as antagonists, but they're only one part of the supernatural landscape and they're as easily portable into a mortals or a mage or vampire chronicle as they are part of Hunter. OK, so they first appeared in Hunter, but so what? <br /> <br /> The most serious objection I have is that they've simply been DONE already. They have an entire book devoted to them, done and finished. And it was a pretty damn good book too. Plenty of good writing, art work, new compacts/conspiracies, archetypal monsters, etc. So, I've already bought that book; do I really need to have to buy a new (reduced) version, again? One that takes up valuable word count (along with another copy of the core rules). Hence, I think we need a slasher chronicle. <br /> <br /> As regards the original Hunter list of antagonists, there are clearly other groups that are woefully under finished, specifically demons and cults. Neither of these had their own books (like in the format of Slasher) and to my mind they are both potentially fecund sources of new material - not to mention the fact that they are laced with plenty of crossover potential (basically almost every supernatural splat has some type of mortal cult nowadays). So yeah, demons and cults, go for it, Onyx, take a chance on something that hasn't been done. We need a cult/demon chronicle, we don't need a slasher chronicle.<br /> <br /> My next objection would be that, to my mind, it's a bit lazy to go for Slashers. The book is done, and I'm worried that they're simply going to be copy over and update slightly the stuff that's already done in 'Slasher'. We might get some new sample antagonists, like the Indigam in Werewolf 2nd ed. but do we really need them? We don't need a Slasher chronicle.<br /> <br /> My next objection is probably toothless but I think its fair. I think slashers have been chosen because they're simply in fashion again at the moment. By this I mean to reference the popularity of Hannibal and True Detective (esp the latter) since these seem to fit the 'average Joe hunter verses almost supernatural' murderers mold. This is all well and good, and it provides some welcome inspiration for modern horror rpg fans, but I'm not sure it's a good reason to base a chronicle on slashers.<br /> <br /> My last objection turns upon the fact that slashers are far to idiosyncratic to base a chronicle on them. The Strix, the Indigam, the Huntsmen, et al, are all bound together by a common metaphysical rubric that is fundamentally connected with their protagonists, while slashers, for the most part, are not. Slashers make their way in the world of darkness without reference to any other entity; they are defined by their need to kill (and perhaps be killed in the end). The link between slashers and hunters is thin and tenuous. Plus I don't like the concept that 'most slashers were hunters who went a bit nuts' idea. Really, does that have to be the case? Does it even make sense? Certainly the archetypal slashers in film and fiction don't seem to suggest that link (Fred Kreuger or Jason as members of a cell? Nah). <br /> <br /> If they want to make slashers work for a chronicle then they're going to have to do some pretty heavy re-engineering so as to make them more than just hunters who start butchering people for crazy reasons (and maybe get ickle supernatural powers). I believe cults and demons would make a far better 'dark mirror' chronicle for hunter than slashers (especially cults).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:32:34-07:00","id":609238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609236#post609236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As regards the original Hunter list of antagonists, there are clearly other groups that are woefully under finished, specifically demons and cults.</div> </div> </div> </div> I still feel bad that I wasn't able to finish the <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/\" target=\"_blank\">cults fanbook</a>. There's some great material in there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:39:12-07:00","id":609241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609238#post609238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still feel bad that I wasn't able to finish the <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/\" target=\"_blank\">cults fanbook</a>. There's some great material in there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed there was; it was/is a great piece of fan-produced material!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:43:25-07:00","id":609243,"title":"","content":"Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T04:32:15-07:00","id":609251,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this makes it more likely that VASCU will be promoted to the main book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:11:35-07:00","id":609269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609236#post609236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most serious objection I have is that they've simply been DONE already.</div> </div> </div> </div> The strix were done twice before Requiem 2e came out - once in Requiem for Rome, once in the Night Horrors book. Idigam were also done in the Night Horrors line. Huntsmen were a 1e core book thing issue in Changeling. Firestorms got a lot of coverage in Promethean.<br /> <br /> The titular characters are the ones that &quot;shake things up.&quot; Strix throw a monkey in the workings of the covenants (not just the wrench, but the entire animal!). Idigiam warp all the sacred prey into unrecognizable horrors. The Huntsmen are the ones that break through the safety nets of the Courts, the Firestorms are the ones that create pandorans and awaken monsters, the Fallen World forces magic to go awry. <br /> <br /> The purpose of the material isn't to introduce new monsters. Its to bring a highlight on an event that undermines everything you think you know about the game. Even if that event is the arrival of a monster, it still completely changes the status quo. Indeed, introducing new monsters would be kind of silly - this is a new edition, the whole point of new editions is to update old material, not introduce new stuff. Its not like any of the other updates introduced anything truly new; it was to catch the core book up with all the changes to the setting all the supplements introduced, and streamline other things. <br /> <br /> Slashers are the mirror-darkly to Hunters and their Vigil - yes, hunters are defined by capturing and killing. Furthermore, Slasher-hood is a common fate for Hunters who've become too monstrous themselves. And you don't think that Slashers won't target Hunters themselves? Or join up with the monsters? You don't see how it challenges the Us Humans versus The Evil Monsters theme in the book? There's a lot here that resonates very strongly with Hunters, and some stuff that I haven't touched on. That's why Slashers were so good in 1e, and why they're getting the title in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> specifically demons and cults. </div> </div> </div> Demons have their chapter in Mortal Remains, same as everyone else. As for a cult? What do you think the Compacts and Conspiracies count as? They're mortal filled organizations with potential antagonist hooks in them. Cancer cells are quire common sources of antagonists as well. They might not have entire books in the Hunter line, but they've both been covered. And that doesn't touch on the fact that both have books outside the Hunter line you can use as resources. If we're going by &quot;already covered by other books,&quot; then demons and cults don't fit either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My next objection is probably toothless but I think its fair. I think slashers have been chosen because they're simply in fashion again at the moment. By this I mean to reference the popularity of Hannibal and True Detective (esp the latter) since these seem to fit the 'average Joe hunter verses almost supernatural' murderers mold. This is all well and good, and it provides some welcome inspiration for modern horror rpg fans, but I'm not sure it's a good reason to base a chronicle on slashers. </div> </div> </div> This is not only toothless, but flat out untrue. Slashers are chosen for more reason than popularity. They're chosen because they fit a thematic story need within the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:46:50-07:00","id":609289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609236#post609236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'm somewhat disappointed that the Hunter chronicle is going to be so antagonist focus - I was hoping for a more open and nuanced appreciation of the setting, its compacts and conspiracies, and the dark mirror of supernatural society that envelopes the Vigil - much like the up coming Mage chronicle.<br /> <br /> Now don't get me wrong, I like slashers as antagonists, but they're only one part of the supernatural landscape and they're as easily portable into a mortals or a mage or vampire chronicle as they are part of Hunter. OK, so they first appeared in Hunter, but so what?<br /> <br /> The most serious objection I have is that they've simply been DONE already. They have an entire book devoted to them, done and finished. And it was a pretty damn good book too. Plenty of good writing, art work, new compacts/conspiracies, archetypal monsters, etc. So, I've already bought that book; do I really need to have to buy a new (reduced) version, again? One that takes up valuable word count (along with another copy of the core rules). Hence, I think we need a slasher chronicle.<br /> <br /> As regards the original Hunter list of antagonists, there are clearly other groups that are woefully under finished, specifically demons and cults. Neither of these had their own books (like in the format of Slasher) and to my mind they are both potentially fecund sources of new material - not to mention the fact that they are laced with plenty of crossover potential (basically almost every supernatural splat has some type of mortal cult nowadays). So yeah, demons and cults, go for it, Onyx, take a chance on something that hasn't been done. We need a cult/demon chronicle, we don't need a slasher chronicle.<br /> <br /> My next objection would be that, to my mind, it's a bit lazy to go for Slashers. The book is done, and I'm worried that they're simply going to be copy over and update slightly the stuff that's already done in 'Slasher'. We might get some new sample antagonists, like the Indigam in Werewolf 2nd ed. but do we really need them? We don't need a Slasher chronicle.<br /> <br /> My next objection is probably toothless but I think its fair. I think slashers have been chosen because they're simply in fashion again at the moment. By this I mean to reference the popularity of Hannibal and True Detective (esp the latter) since these seem to fit the 'average Joe hunter verses almost supernatural' murderers mold. This is all well and good, and it provides some welcome inspiration for modern horror rpg fans, but I'm not sure it's a good reason to base a chronicle on slashers.<br /> <br /> My last objection turns upon the fact that slashers are far to idiosyncratic to base a chronicle on them. The Strix, the Indigam, the Huntsmen, et al, are all bound together by a common metaphysical rubric that is fundamentally connected with their protagonists, while slashers, for the most part, are not. Slashers make their way in the world of darkness without reference to any other entity; they are defined by their need to kill (and perhaps be killed in the end). The link between slashers and hunters is thin and tenuous. Plus I don't like the concept that 'most slashers were hunters who went a bit nuts' idea. Really, does that have to be the case? Does it even make sense? Certainly the archetypal slashers in film and fiction don't seem to suggest that link (Fred Kreuger or Jason as members of a cell? Nah).<br /> <br /> If they want to make slashers work for a chronicle then they're going to have to do some pretty heavy re-engineering so as to make them more than just hunters who start butchering people for crazy reasons (and maybe get ickle supernatural powers). I believe cults and demons would make a far better 'dark mirror' chronicle for hunter than slashers (especially cults).</div> </div> </div> </div>Several objections to the objections:<br /> <br /> First, Slashers <i>are </i>a dark mirror to hunters, it's called out even in the book. Hunters are by nature killers by necessity (at the very least); even the Loyalists of Thule all know how to operate a gun. A Slasher is what happens when they stop caring about the necessity and start killing because their ideology tells them to, or simply because it's the only thing they're good at anymore. All the rage and pain that creates a hunter, but none of the ethics or focus. Even their abilities reflect this-they don't so much gain preternatural skill as an assassin so much as the fact that they no longer have moral limits, which also turns off their mortal limitations. Not every Slasher was once a Hunter, but enough of them were to remind the Vigil that the candle flame can become an all-consuming wildfire if they forget why they lit it.<br /> <br /> Second: cults already have a lot of focus in the nWoD 2E in the core, there's even a merit signifying membership in one with supernatural mojo. Making them the focus of the Chronicle would retread the book you buy to have a context for Hunter 2E to begin with. On the other hand, Hunter demons are, quite simply, <i>boring. </i>Not because you can't get stories from them, but because they are made for a very specific genre of stories; temptation. All well and good for anyone not a demon, but demons themselves, simply by occupying that niche? Can't really have a character themselves anymore, just an echo of a particular type of temptation (even Mr. White; all he's good at is murder investigations and asking the question if someone is willing to commit murder to solve a murder-the only thing sympathetic on a human level is his confusion as to whether his human identity was his original one, and it's pointed out it really doesn't matter that much to him). A Slasher also has a defining action, but killing and managing to get away with it contains within it the seeds for many different genres; victimization, action, investigation, politics (a clever and manipulative killer disguising their hunger for any death as death of a hated minority-which means manipulating their supporters out of the way). That, and there's a reason serial killers end up the villains so often-how a seemingly normal individual loses all aversion to death and violence is fascinating, and probably unique to each person.<br /> <br /> Third, the book is there. It's also 1E, and linked to a system that no longer exists and its replacement has completely different context (a Slasher may have any Integrity-low Integrity means their drive for death is born from trauma, a high Integrity means they're so calloused they don't care any more). That, and Avengers need an update. And probably need rules for truly supernatural abilities too instead of just the two-or-four they're born with. And if &quot;already been done&quot; was honestly a problem, we wouldn't have 2E to begin with. Certainly not the Strix, whose B&amp;S version is their <i>third </i>incarnation. And VASCU deserves to be in the core.<br /> <br /> Fourth, if you really want cults and demons, there's other supplements to Hunter in the pipeline. Those two things probably deserve a book of their own, rather than Major Splat Under Hunter Rules books (although those books are pretty good, I'll admit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 07-31-2015, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:47:39-07:00","id":609290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>123456789blaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=608508#post608508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To everyone: what do you believe Hunter is about as a major gameline? What is its focus? What makes it cool and interesting and special to you?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>To me, it's humanity biting back. Which doesn't need to mean taking a shotgun and packing it with silver rounds. It may be research and an attempt at understanding. It may be trying to steal the supernaturals' secrets to use against them. It may be trying to reason with them. It may be trying to blow the whole thing wide open and show everyone what the world is really like. But one way or the other, it's about normal humans opening their eyes, or having them torn open, and deciding to take a stand. And reminding the supernaturals, often painfully, that they're not cattle. Not all of them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:58:00-07:00","id":609296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609289#post609289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, Slashers <i>are </i>a dark mirror to hunters, it's called out even in the book. Hunters are by nature killers by necessity (at the very least); even the Loyalists of Thule all know how to operate a gun. A Slasher is what happens when they stop caring about the necessity and start killing because their ideology tells them to, or simply because it's the only thing they're good at anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree actually.<br /> <br /> Slashers have many parallels to hunters, but they lack one key trait that's nessacary for them to be a Dark Mirror - Hunters work in teams, Slashers, well they have special rules for solo tactics.<br /> <br /> Cults are a truer Dark Mirror IMO. (Hence why I did try to write a book on the subject)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:02:11-07:00","id":609449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609296#post609296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree actually.<br /> <br /> Slashers have many parallels to hunters, but they lack one key trait that's nessacary for them to be a Dark Mirror - Hunters work in teams, Slashers, well they have special rules for solo tactics.<br /> <br /> Cults are a truer Dark Mirror IMO. (Hence why I did try to write a book on the subject)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I can't disagree with that. But I can say that it plays into the idea of the one true difference between Slashers and Hunters; Hunters still have empathy, still have a life out of the flame of the candle. Which means they can still work as a team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:14:53-07:00","id":609463,"title":"","content":"There's an intimate connection between hunters and slashers, at least as far as the rules are concerned: slashers are built exactly the same way that hunters are, except that the element of the hunter \u201ctemplate\u201d that's touted as the thing that keeps him human and sane (his Profession) is replaced by an element that <i>separates</i> him from humanity and turns him into a monster (his Undertaking).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:20:41-07:00","id":609468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609269#post609269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The strix were done twice before Requiem 2e came out - once in Requiem for Rome, once in the Night Horrors book. Idigam were also done in the Night Horrors line. Huntsmen were a 1e core book thing issue in Changeling. Firestorms got a lot of coverage in Promethean.<br /> <br /> The titular characters are the ones that &quot;shake things up.&quot; Strix throw a monkey in the workings of the covenants (not just the wrench, but the entire animal!). Idigiam warp all the sacred prey into unrecognizable horrors. The Huntsmen are the ones that break through the safety nets of the Courts, the Firestorms are the ones that create pandorans and awaken monsters, the Fallen World forces magic to go awry.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the material isn't to introduce new monsters. Its to bring a highlight on an event that undermines everything you think you know about the game. Even if that event is the arrival of a monster, it still completely changes the status quo. Indeed, introducing new monsters would be kind of silly - this is a new edition, the whole point of new editions is to update old material, not introduce new stuff. Its not like any of the other updates introduced anything truly new; it was to catch the core book up with all the changes to the setting all the supplements introduced, and streamline other things.<br /> <br /> Slashers are the mirror-darkly to Hunters and their Vigil - yes, hunters are defined by capturing and killing. Furthermore, Slasher-hood is a common fate for Hunters who've become too monstrous themselves. And you don't think that Slashers won't target Hunters themselves? Or join up with the monsters? You don't see how it challenges the Us Humans versus The Evil Monsters theme in the book? There's a lot here that resonates very strongly with Hunters, and some stuff that I haven't touched on. That's why Slashers were so good in 1e, and why they're getting the title in 2e.<br /> <br /> Demons have their chapter in Mortal Remains, same as everyone else. As for a cult? What do you think the Compacts and Conspiracies count as? They're mortal filled organizations with potential antagonist hooks in them. Cancer cells are quire common sources of antagonists as well. They might not have entire books in the Hunter line, but they've both been covered. And that doesn't touch on the fact that both have books outside the Hunter line you can use as resources. If we're going by &quot;already covered by other books,&quot; then demons and cults don't fit either.<br /> <br /> This is not only toothless, but flat out untrue. Slashers are chosen for more reason than popularity. They're chosen because they fit a thematic story need within the genre.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, yeah, you're entirely correct, MCN. But it seemed to me that those cases (such as the Indigam and the Strix), were parts of larger supplements that were expanded upon more fully in their respective chronicle book. The Slashers weren't just a chapter in a supplment, they were in the core and they had a large thick tome to themselves already. Hence why, to my subjective eye, they seemed complete whereas demons (as distinct from 'Descent Demons' or 'Daemons' as I like to refer to them) and cults were either incomplete or mechanical/thematically inconsistent. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The problem is, for me, that basically everything 'paranormal' that a hunter encounters is a 'shake up' of one qualitative form or another. You've got all the myriad entities that we players can assign to a splat box as well as all those other 'anomalies' that defy easy classifications - all those errant dreams of the Dark Mother so to speak! </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For me, looking back, I do think that the new presentations did introduce something new to their antagonists. The Strix in particular became a reoccurring plague of vampire boogiemen rather than just the antagonists of the Julii or a monster in a supplement. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm that's a good point. I do appreciate the subversion of the 'Hunter humans verses monstrous Other' trope, and I acknowledge that Slasher do perform that role well, but it doesn't deflect that they already did that in Slashers (and did it well), nor that there are other ways to do this that are just as good, cults being one of them, and one without a supplement book (or even a chapter) of their own. Plus I'd query the Hunter Fate bit a bit. For me, Slashers are just one facet of the Dark Mirror that hunters must experience. Humanity is warped and mutilated in all sorts of ways by its interaction with the paranormal, and hunters do become slashers. But I strongly believe that the slasher doesn't make a good reflection for the majority of hunters, at least not the ones that have existed in my chronicles (and despite the relatively infrequent requests to play a slasher!). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh don't get me started on that Demon chapter! Suffice to say I think the richness of the demon type antagonist was poorly handled in that chapter. Arguably, I don't think that the compacts and conspiracies in themselves, nor the possibility of cancer cells, is the same as the rich concept of a cult - hence why they're not conflated in the core book. Cults are far more nuanced, deeper in form and possibility than compacts and conspiracies, and (going back to the dark mirror bit) they should function as a nightmarish reflection or antithesis to the hunter vigil and its shadowy organisations. Cults represent a surrendering to the dark forces that predate upon the human spirit, the parasites and monsters that threaten to tear humanity apart and leave something tainted and monstrous to feed on the remnants of their former kin (the 'In the Mouth of madness' apocalypse scenario). Cults are the anti-vigil, whereas a slasher is the dark reflection of just one type/facet of the hunter saga.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:30:47-07:00","id":609477,"title":"","content":"On reflection, I can perhaps see a logic to using slashers as the antagonist of a chronicle style book - you need something that can be introduced/used relatively easily and without massive amounts of supporting material. Plus if you want to follow the template of the Strix and Indigam chronicles, you need a rogues gallery of antagonists that can be presented in short, punchy vignettes. Cults would arguably require a lot more structural support in terms of rules and story telling than Slashers.<br /> <br /> But I do worry that making slashers the central-ish 'big bad' of the default Hunter chronicle is not the best idea in the world. I think demons (of the spiritual variety) would fill that role just as well. Not to mention that their intimate connection with human history, religion and folklore make them an iconic form of evil that practically any Hunter culture (past or present) can resonant with - slashers seem just a tad too recent in their pedigree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:34:51-07:00","id":609480,"title":"","content":"The main problem with cults is that they usually are symptoms, not the cause. Cults happen because someone (or something) cause them to happen. When you add a new cult to your game, you usually need to think about everything that surrounds it- where they came from, what they search for, what motivates them. Usually, it ends up either with them crossing to another line (vampire/idigam/mummy/demon/abyssal/etc cults)or making them into a group of madmen, which is more or less Slasher with a twist. Cults are just everywhere- there is no single gameline which can claim them as their own &quot;thing&quot;. Slashers, however, are something which is very &quot;Huntery&quot;- they belong to the Vigil world, and don't require much work to add them to any Chronicle. Just add water (or blood) and walla! an instant antagonist! Plus, I think that an antagonist chapter for Cults would devour more wordcount than a black hole, which could be used for better uses.<br /> <br /> EDIT- ninjad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:41:00-07:00","id":609515,"title":"","content":"As I see it, different hunters will fight different monsters, for different reasons and with different methods. A hunter might spend their entire career stealing secrets from magicians and warlocks, never facing any living dead or lycantrophe. Another might be your stereotypical vampire hunter, putting stakes in bloodsuckers without caring for anything else. But becoming a Slasher is something that can happen to any of them. The line between the burning dedication to the Vigil and destructive insanity is razor-thin. Losing yourself to the hunt and becoming just another kind of monster is a universal threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:07:50-07:00","id":609537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609289#post609289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several objections to the objections:<br /> <br /> First, Slashers <i>are </i>a dark mirror to hunters, it's called out even in the book. Hunters are by nature killers by necessity (at the very least); even the Loyalists of Thule all know how to operate a gun. A Slasher is what happens when they stop caring about the necessity and start killing because their ideology tells them to, or simply because it's the only thing they're good at anymore. All the rage and pain that creates a hunter, but none of the ethics or focus. Even their abilities reflect this-they don't so much gain preternatural skill as an assassin so much as the fact that they no longer have moral limits, which also turns off their mortal limitations. Not every Slasher was once a Hunter, but enough of them were to remind the Vigil that the candle flame can become an all-consuming wildfire if they forget why they lit it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I would argue that they are <b><i>a</i></b> dark mirror to some versions of the hunter storyline, not <i><b>the</b></i> dark mirror. I can bite necks and abduct people behind my garden hedge (I don't) but that doesn't mean that I possess some qualitative sympathy with vampire and the True Fae. Nor do I think that its entirely right to say that the slasher lies at the end of the hunter road as a likely end point for every one who takes up the vigil. The fact that slashers <i>are</i> monsters and their prey are mortal humans for the most part and not some type of monster, highlights for me the problematic nature of the dark mirror theory. It just doesn't ring true for the majority of hunter characters I have GMed. I don't even think that a significant minority of slasher even were once hunters.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second: cults already have a lot of focus in the nWoD 2E in the core, there's even a merit signifying membership in one with supernatural mojo. Making them the focus of the Chronicle would retread the book you buy to have a context for Hunter 2E to begin with. On the other hand, Hunter demons are, quite simply, <i>boring. </i>Not because you can't get stories from them, but because they are made for a very specific genre of stories; temptation. All well and good for anyone not a demon, but demons themselves, simply by occupying that niche? Can't really have a character themselves anymore, just an echo of a particular type of temptation (even Mr. White; all he's good at is murder investigations and asking the question if someone is willing to commit murder to solve a murder-the only thing sympathetic on a human level is his confusion as to whether his human identity was his original one, and it's pointed out it really doesn't matter that much to him). A Slasher also has a defining action, but killing and managing to get away with it contains within it the seeds for many different genres; victimization, action, investigation, politics (a clever and manipulative killer disguising their hunger for any death as death of a hated minority-which means manipulating their supporters out of the way). That, and there's a reason serial killers end up the villains so often-how a seemingly normal individual loses all aversion to death and violence is fascinating, and probably unique to each person. </div> </div> </div>The hunter demons are a little flat, but that's more to do with the brevity of their section than anything else. I mean the slasher and vampire sections aren't exactly inspirational either and its not to we get the supplements that they really shine. I think temptation is a strong theme for demons (so is corruption, transcendence through evil and individuality, decadence and perversity for it own sake), but it's definitely not the sole defining theme of these evil spirits, especially if you look across cultures and at other dark and inhuman spirits of evil. But temptation is certainly a strong enough theme to light a fire with, so to speak. Demons, via their multiplicity of themes and agendas can access the same genres as any slasher, inc those you listed above. In fact, I think slashers are far more limited than demons, as in their fullest definition as evil spirits of the Lower Depths, their natures can be legion, if you excuse the pun. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third, the book is there. It's also 1E, and linked to a system that no longer exists and its replacement has completely different context (a Slasher may have any Integrity-low Integrity means their drive for death is born from trauma, a high Integrity means they're so calloused they don't care any more). That, and Avengers need an update. And probably need rules for truly supernatural abilities too instead of just the two-or-four they're born with. And if &quot;already been done&quot; was honestly a problem, we wouldn't have 2E to begin with. Certainly not the Strix, whose B&amp;S version is their <i>third </i>incarnation. And VASCU deserves to be in the core. </div> </div> </div>You won't be surprised if I disagree with you, partially. The rules do indeed need a good update, as Integrity is certainly a difficult one to adapt to slashers. But the fact that the core rules have changed doesn't make 'already done' a problem. Updates and improvements are always welcome. I just think cults and demons are a more pressing update since they've been neglected in the past and are a more significant gap. I mean, I can and have made up slashers with just the new MR rules updates and the new endowments. Integrity is not a great issue for my antagonist designs as it is for the player characters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth, if you really want cults and demons, there's other supplements to Hunter in the pipeline. Those two things probably deserve a book of their own, rather than Major Splat Under Hunter Rules books (although those books are pretty good, I'll admit). </div> </div> </div>Outstanding. I certainly agree with you regarding the separate books. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:17:20-07:00","id":609551,"title":"","content":"For me, a big thing about why Slashers work as <i>the</i> cart upsetter has a little more practical edge to it on top of everything else. The biggest advantage a cell, of any sort, has is co-ordianation. Sure, numbers and allies help, but those numbers require trust. Cancer cells are the most dangerous things that can happen to hunters because they sneak in and fuck that all up. Slashers? They are fucking cancer. THey can come from outside easily enough, they can also come from within at any point. Even scourges are still nominally human, so it can be so easy to trust them, to trust their essential humanity.<br /> <br /> Every question put to them, though, suggests that humanity as a whole has a self-destruct button it's just eager to push. Slashers break the subtle transition from hunting to murdering and paint (figuratively speaking) everyone as a target.<br /> <br /> You trust the people around you, and you could take the night.<br /> You trust the people around you, and you could be in pieces by the morn.<br /> How clearly can you see with your flimsy light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-31-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:22:51-07:00","id":609582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609078#post609078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Hunter was something of a minor template(-ish?) thing in the past, but I'm hoping it will step up a bit as a major template. Alternate Integrity seems like the perfect way to handle the Tells, and a divide between normal life and Vigil seems like a good way to contrast that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically <b>does not</b> want hunters to be Major Template, rather to be clearly Lesser Template. The whole beauty of playing hunter is that you are <i>still</i> human ( and from Tier is based what &quot;still&quot; means ), but does inhuman things - killing persons, stealing knowledge, slow but steady ride down on your Integrity, down to becoming Slasher.<br /> <br /> Also, you cannot mix Major with Lesser Templetes, and I want to have mine Sleepwalker, Wolf-Blooded and a like Hunters, especially as 2ED other corebooks are pointing their Lesser Templertes as typical witch or werewolf hunters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What I <b>do like to see</b> that characters still have Integrity ( as they are mostly human ), but can break Masqueraded/Delirium/Sleeping Curse and Risk Willpower from the beginning of their Vigil. Basically, that when mortal &quot;becomes&quot; hunter after first contact with supernatural, he becomes immune ( or at least resistant ) to &quot;<i><b>forgetting about supernatural</b></i>&quot;. Being hunter is to have eyes wide open, even if you see only darkness all around you, candle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609078#post609078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- review every organization, and don't be afraid to make a compact into a conspiracy or vice-versa. The 2 major differences compacts vs conspiracies were: scope and Endowments. Now Compacts are also getting Endowments, so that doesn't matter, and even scope was pretty iffy to be honest, since we had at least a few global compacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can whole hearty agree to - we need new division on what is Compact and what is Conspiracy, as both groups have Endowments now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:04:31-07:00","id":609659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609468#post609468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, yeah, you're entirely correct, MCN. But it seemed to me that those cases (such as the Indigam and the Strix), were parts of larger supplements that were expanded upon more fully in their respective chronicle book. The Slashers weren't just a chapter in a supplment, they were in the core and they had a large thick tome to themselves already. Hence why, to my subjective eye, they seemed complete whereas demons (as distinct from 'Descent Demons' or 'Daemons' as I like to refer to them) and cults were either incomplete or mechanical/thematically inconsistent. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> But that's just it - the amount of coverage in 1e is immaterial. What matters how it relates to 2e, and how the game has evolved since the core came out. This isn't new material. This is an update to the core book material. The focus, almost by definition, must be on something that's been covered before.<br /> <br /> In the specific case of Hunter and demon kind, its very likely we'll see less focus on them in the Hunter core going forwards. Both Inferno and Descent are separate games, one for the WoD core, one for its own gameline. I get that you don't like how its treated, but it seems that demons are just moving towards a non-hunter specific thing. They're just one category that's being hunted, alongside vamp, were, mage, 'ling, prommie, 'eater, mummy, and so on. The game's evolved to give them less of a focus than the core, it seems, so I bet that's going to be reflected in the new game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The problem is, for me, that basically everything 'paranormal' that a hunter encounters is a 'shake up' of one qualitative form or another. You've got all the myriad entities that we players can assign to a splat box as well as all those other 'anomalies' that defy easy classifications - all those errant dreams of the Dark Mother so to speak! </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> Ish. All the other antagonists that hunters face, in one form or another, are no longer humans. Even mages are no longer humans, but mental-based monsters. Slashers are, for all intents and purposes, still very much humans. That's what I mean by &quot;shaking it up.&quot; The default is to hunt down monsters, find out their weaknesses and habits. Slashers defy that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:12:19-07:00","id":609668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609537#post609537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can bite necks and abduct people behind my garden hedge (I don't) but that doesn't mean that I possess some qualitative sympathy with vampire and the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood bathers definitely have qualitative sympathy, as you put it, with vampires. Abducting, abusing, and dressing your victims up in outfits so you can project things on them would create sympathy with the Fae. Strawmen arguments are strawmen. Biting necks isn't what makes vampires, well, vampires. Its the absorption of life energy, be it through blood, breath, or other means, that does it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:53:01-07:00","id":609801,"title":"","content":"&quot;In short, Hunter is a game about Light and Shadows, answers and questions. It doesn't matter if you are a lone hunter in the night, if you have the backup of your friends with you or even if you are a child of the devil or a drug kingpin or a semi-cannibalistic monster eater. The only thing that matters is that you take a stand and step into the night, willing to endanger your own soul in order to drive away the darkness. &quot;<br /> <br /> Well said.<br /> <br /> Any idea on who's developing Hunter 2nd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:10:54-07:00","id":609925,"title":"","content":"From GMC:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Is it possible for a character to reach a point where killing another human being is not a breaking point? Players might make the argument for soldiers, policemen, gang members or good-hearted serial killers to be exempt from suffering breaking points from taking a life, up to a point. For mortal, non-supernatural characters, our recommendation is that if a character kills a person, it's always a breaking point, even if the player gets a positive modifier to the roll.</span></div><br /> This, I think, it where the line between Hunter and Slasher is drawn: once a hunter gets to the point that he no longer suffers Breaking Points for killing people, he's a Slasher and should choose an Undertaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:14:44-07:00","id":609929,"title":"","content":"That's how I've always thought it should go. Obviously monster's aren't people in this context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:55:17-07:00","id":610526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609582#post609582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This I can whole hearty agree to - we need new division on what is Compact and what is Conspiracy, as both groups have Endowments now.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait.. are we talking about a Compacts &amp; Conspiracies kind of Endowments or about the real deal? Because if it is the later, when and where it was stated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T01:57:46-07:00","id":610568,"title":"","content":"I think what wyrdhamster meant was that the name &quot;compact&quot; and &quot;conspiracy&quot; should be independant of what kind of Endowment they have. For example, Les Mysteries has no organisation whatsoever - so perhaps despite it's Endowment it should be a Compact.<br /> <br /> That I agree with strongly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:03:33-07:00","id":610571,"title":"","content":"What King writes - now all Hunter factions can have Endowments and so division on Compact and Conspiracy should be based on more their real world power(?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-01-2015, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:29:03-07:00","id":610628,"title":"","content":"I meant about the &quot;now&quot; thing- is the &quot;now&quot; the &quot;now from the book C&amp;C or is it some new info was released?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:18:36-07:00","id":610786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=610628#post610628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant about the &quot;now&quot; thing- is the &quot;now&quot; the &quot;now from the book C&amp;C or is it some new info was released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just C&amp;C, but the extrapolation is reasonable. Personally, since Tier has been more firmly defined as what's at stake in the 2nd edition games, I've come round to thinking there's no point in distinguishing between compacts and conspiracies at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:50:44-07:00","id":611387,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm hoping that 2e steers clear of the \u201ctier 1/2/3\u201d terminology. Speak of independent cells, of compacts and of conspiracies; speak of Endowments and how they come in two varieties: supernatural Endowments such as Advanced Armoury, Benedictions, Castigations, Elixirs, Relics, or Thaumatechnology; and temporal Endowments such as the Bacchanal, Prayer, Unearthed Secrets, the All-Seeing Eye, I'm Doing Science, or Your Friends and Neighbors. Where Tier gets mentioned at all, use the terminology provided in <b>GMC</b>: you have Local, Regional, Global, or Cosmic, not \u201cTier 1, Tier 2, Tier 3, Tier 4\u201d \u2014 and even here, I\u2019d steer clear of actually using the T-word, instead speaking of a chronicle's scope. <br /> <br /> And then talk about how these things interrelate, which (in a nutshell) should be all about <i>tendencies</i>, and never about lock-step bindings. Independent cells are most at home when the chronicle's scope is local; but there's nothing wrong with an independent cell tackling a global or even cosmic chronicle to the best of their ability. Likewise, conspiracies <i>tend to</i> operate on the global stage; but a TFV cell operating in a town and dealing primarily with local concerns is a perfectly viable approach. <br /> <br /> Supernatural Endowments <i>tend to be</i> in the Conspiracies\u2019 wheelhouse, and temporal Endowments <i>tend to be</i> something Compacts have; but go with what makes sense rather than holding fast to these associations: as The King's Raven has mentioned, Les Mysteres makes more sense as a Compact despite being built around a supernatural Endowment; and the Loyalists of Thule have always struck me as being a global conspiracy despite not technically having a supernatural Endowment*. Heck, I'd have no problem with an individual hunter who is sufficiently religiously motivated having the Prayer Endowment even if she has never heard of, or is fundamentally opposed to, the Long Night, or for an Ascended One to lack Elixirs (either because he hasn't developed them yet or because he's more interested in the uses of pharmacy). <br /> <br /> Again, <i>tendencies</i>, not <i>mandates</i>. <br /> <br /> <hr />* Though technically, their heightened access to magical rituals such as found in <b>Second Sight</b>, <b>Witch Hunters</b>, or <b>Summoners</b> could be thought of as a supernatural Endowment every bit as much as the Aegis Kai Doru\u2019s Relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-01-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:19:09-07:00","id":611400,"title":"","content":"my two cents on the matter are that either you turn Endowments into real &quot;powers&quot;, like Disciplines and Gifts so that under certain circumstances any hunter could buy them, or that you keep the &quot;only conspiracies have access to Endowments- and even than only one Endowment per group&quot;. Again, it depends on what you want Endowments to be. If you want them to be the kind of tricks and techniques an hunter learn in order to advance the Vigil, take the former. If you want them to represent a special resource an organization has after generations of research and accumulated knowledge, take the later. Either you divorce the Endowments from the orgs entirely or that you maintain a rigid status que. Giving certain groups Endowments and others not just because would feel for me like doing only half job and ends up with me eventually saying &quot;why those groups are &quot;lesser&quot; than those?&quot;<br /> <br /> Eventually, it seems that the main complain is that certain compacts feel like they should have supernatural powers, and that certain conspiracies feel like they should work in a smaller scale. There is no one who thinks that there is a canon conspiracy who should lose access to Endowments. If it was up to me, everyone would have got Endowments (and I mean the real deal, not that semi thingy from C&amp;C which I find as boring and waste of wordcount. I think that they should work as Tactics of some kind, and save the title Endowment for the more serious abilities of the hunters). I also think that the Tiers (and there is nothing wrong with that word, IMO) should be revised a little- but not too much. They should represent the reach of the organization, and its level of influence- not the number of hunters in the group, but how important it i in the world.<br /> <br /> In short, I find the creation of conspiracies without Endowments as they work now as boring, and unless you divorce the two entirely and allow even a 1st tier hunter to learn something like Castigations the current paradigm should be kept- and that most of all, the 2nd ed should decide what is the meaning of Endowments: either they are Kewl Powerz or that they represent the sum of a conspiracy's resources. Only after that you should start thinking about the different groups and on which Tier they should operate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:10:29-07:00","id":611434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611400#post611400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my two cents on the matter are that either you turn Endowments into real \u201cpowers\u201d, like Disciplines and Gifts so that under certain circumstances any hunter could buy them, or that you keep the \u201conly conspiracies have access to Endowments- and even than only one Endowment per group\u201d. Again, it depends on what you want Endowments to be. If you want them to be the kind of tricks and techniques an hunter learn in order to advance the Vigil, take the former. If you want them to represent a special resource an organization has after generations of research and accumulated knowledge, take the later. Either you divorce the Endowments from the orgs entirely or that you maintain a rigid status que. Giving certain groups Endowments and others not just because would feel for me like doing only half job and ends up with me eventually saying \u201cwhy those groups are \u2018lesser\u2019 than those?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as a false dichotomy: either we must divorce supernatural Endowments entirely from Conspiracies or we must bind them together exclusively? No room for any sort of middle ground? Sorry; even as presented in 1e, I don\u2019t see why (e.g.) Relics should be the <i>exclusive</i> domain of the Aegis Kai Doru; but I <i>do</i> see why that Conspiracy should have easier access to Relics than, say, lone hunters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611400#post611400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually, it seems that the main complain is that certain compacts feel like they should have supernatural powers, and that certain conspiracies feel like they should work in a smaller scale. There is no one who thinks that there is a canon conspiracy who should lose access to Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. My mention of promoting the Loyalists of Thule to Conspiracy status wasn't motivated by their already-established access to supernatural rituals; indeed, I\u2019d rather <i>not</i> have their rituals recast as a supernatural Endowment, as that tends to encourage the notion that you make a Loyalist in order to gain access to their rituals \u2014 which is the <i>opposite</i> of how they should be portrayed: Loyalists are primarily information brokers, and any rituals they might know are side effects of their investigations \u2014 and generally viewed as <i>dangerous secrets</i> to be used only as a last resort. The motivation for calling them a Conspiracy is that the Loyalists of Thule strike me as being an org that operates on a global scale and tend to be well organized. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611400#post611400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was up to me, everyone would have got Endowments (and I mean the real deal, not that semi thingy from C&amp;C which I find as boring and waste of wordcount. I think that they should work as Tactics of some kind, and save the title Endowment for the more serious abilities of the hunters).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. Prayer, in particular, doesn't strike me as being suitable as a Tactic; and while it isn't supernatural the way Benedictions are, it definitely feels like an Endowment to me. But the same holds true of most of the temporal Endowments that C&amp;C introduced. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611400#post611400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the Tiers (and there is nothing wrong with that word, IMO) should be revised a little- but not too much. They should represent the reach of the organization, and its level of influence- not the number of hunters in the group, but how important it is in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with \u201cTier\u201d is that it brings unnecessary baggage to the discussion. I agree that the distinction between the various types of hunter orgs (that is, cells, compacts, and conspiracies) should primarily be about the reach of the org and its level of influence; but you don't need to use terms like \u201ctier one\u201d or \u201ctier three\u201d to convey that point. Just note that conspiracies tend to have a more global reach and influence than compacts, which in turn have more reach than independent cells. <br /> <br /> EDIT: it's similar to how Mage 1e made extensive references to Atlantis, whereas Mage 2e is restricting all Atlantis references to a single Appendix devoted to the topic. Atlantis ended up being a needlessly divisive (and largely misunderstood) concept in Mage, and the second edition mostly removed it; I'm saying that the \u201cTier\u201d terminology has likewise become a stumbling block that we're probably better off without. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611400#post611400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, I find the creation of conspiracies without Endowments as they work now as boring, and unless you divorce the two entirely and allow even a 1st tier hunter to learn something like Castigations the current paradigm should be kept- and that most of all, the 2nd ed should decide what is the meaning of Endowments: either they are Kewl Powerz or that they represent the sum of a conspiracy's resources. Only after that you should start thinking about the different groups and on which Tier they should operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you view Conspiracies primarily as a means of accessing supernatural powers, then yes, a Conspiracy without access to supernatural Endowments would be pointless. Frankly though, I think it does Conspiracies a disservice to view them so narrowly. In most (maybe all?) cases, there should be enough substance to the conspiracy that one could play an interesting game featuring members who <i>don't</i> have access to its supernatural Endowments. If there isn't already, the conspiracy should be revised so that there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-01-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T00:19:29-07:00","id":611950,"title":"","content":"Like I've said, that's just how I view the subject- I know it is not a popular view, but this is my opinion. I don't want a &quot;middle ground&quot; for separating between Endowments and Conspiracies- either you do it or not. Feel free to disagree (and I know that many would disagree) but the point is that I've never felt compelled to play with compacts, so I can't understand why would anyone want to see a conspiracy without an Endowment or lowering certain conspiracies to that tier. If anything, I hope that the new edition would make the gap between the tiers a bit closer- that is, Conspiracies would be more localized and compacts will have more reach. After that, if ti was up to me, I would have given everyone access to Endowments by either divorcing them entirely from the orgs or simply giving each org its own power. That's it.<br /> <br /> Like I've said before, I know it is not a popular opinion and that many people do like compacts as groups who lack special Endowments. Everyone free to disagree with me, but it is just how I think hunter should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T01:14:12-07:00","id":611961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then talk about how these things interrelate, which (in a nutshell) should be all about <i>tendencies</i>, and never about lock-step bindings. Independent cells are most at home when the chronicle's scope is local; but there's nothing wrong with an independent cell tackling a global or even cosmic chronicle to the best of their ability. Likewise, conspiracies <i>tend to</i> operate on the global stage; but a TFV cell operating in a town and dealing primarily with local concerns is a perfectly viable approach.</div> </div> </div> </div> Apart from the fact I'm generally ok with using the T-word (along with Scope and Mojo). This is what I've been saying for a very long time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Loyalists of Thule have always struck me as being a global conspiracy despite not technically having a supernatural Endowment</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yes. Same with the Barrett Comission and possibly Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Heck, I'd have no problem with an individual hunter who is sufficiently religiously motivated having the Prayer Endowment even if she has never heard of, or is fundamentally opposed to, the Long Night</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed on the Prayer. Religious motivations are <i>such</i> a common idea for Hunters (Ahl al-Jabal, Long Night, Ascending Ones-Knife of Paradise, The Faithful of Shulpae, Knights of Saint George, Les Mysteres, Malleus Maleficarum, and possibly some Lucifuge) that I think The Prayer should be a Merit not an Endowment.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what I'd give the Long Night<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or for an Ascended One to lack Elixirs (either because he hasn't developed them yet or because he's more interested in the uses of pharmacy).</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically there's no rule saying you have to buy dots in Elixir so this is covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though technically, their heightened access to magical rituals such as found in <b>Second Sight</b>, <b>Witch Hunters</b>, or <b>Summoners</b> could be thought of as a supernatural Endowment every bit as much as the Aegis Kai Doru\u2019s Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>After agreeing with most of what you're saying I'm going to disagree here <b>very very</b> strongly.<br /> <br /> To me a supernatural Endowment is not &quot;magic powers&quot;, it's &quot;an institutional ability to teach magical powers to your members&quot;.<br /> <br /> Second Sight powers, well the Low Magic chapter talks at length about how hard it is to learn Thamaturgy. The Malleus Maleficarum can take a cop with no higher education and teach him to use Benedictions in whatever hours he can find between the job and his family commitments.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Malleus Maleficarum also has some Thamaturges who practice catholic Theurgy. But the pass rate for &quot;Theurgy school&quot; is probably below ten percent, and you need to have great grades from the semenary even before you can even get into the door.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611434#post611434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as a false dichotomy: either we must divorce supernatural Endowments entirely from Conspiracies or we must bind them together exclusively? No room for any sort of middle ground? Sorry; even as presented in 1e, I don\u2019t see why (e.g.) Relics should be the <i>exclusive</i> domain of the Aegis Kai Doru; but I <i>do</i> see why that Conspiracy should have easier access to Relics than, say, lone hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I agree with you about Relics, the MM has got to have some Saint's bones around, I do think that - for example: Benediction is the exclusive domain of the Malleus Maleficarum.<br /> <br /> In fact I think most of the current Endowments would be exclusive to their current groups. Relics is the exception (and Arragements if you count fanwork).<br /> <br /> That said, I agree with your broader point. The Loyalists of Thule should be a Conspiracy without any Endowment. Les Mysteries should be a Compact with an Endowment (and reworked with a narrower religious focus than that nonsensical omni-shamanism).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=611387#post611387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have to disagree. Prayer, in particular, doesn't strike me as being suitable as a Tactic; and while it isn't supernatural the way Benedictions are, it definitely feels like an Endowment to me. But the same holds true of most of the temporal Endowments that C&amp;C introduced.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually Prayer as a tactic makes great sense to me - though it might be redundant next to Moral Support.<br /> <br /> What's your objection to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T05:37:42-07:00","id":613246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=609801#post609801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any idea on who's developing Hunter 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Monica Valentinelli is the developer for Hunter 2E.<br /> <br /> She previously worked on Hunter: Mortal Remains (writing and editing), she wrote Hunter: Doubting Souls for Dark Eras, she co-wrote Dread Names Red List for V20 with me. Outside of OPP she developed the Firefly RPG for Margaret Weis Productions, has written for Unknown Armies, All Flesh Must Be Eaten, Mistborn, Alethea, and Eclipse Phase to name a few.<br /> <br /> MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:04:50-07:00","id":613258,"title":"","content":"really? I'm happy yo hear that. I like her work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:06:18-07:00","id":613600,"title":"","content":"Me too, Doubting Souls was my favorite of the stock Dark Eras, and I've enjoyed the Red List too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:19:20-07:00","id":613614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/608026-hunter-2nd-edition-the-slasher-chronicles?p=613246#post613246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Monica Valentinelli is the developer for Hunter 2E.<br /> <br /> She previously worked on Hunter: Mortal Remains (writing and editing), she wrote Hunter: Doubting Souls for Dark Eras, she co-wrote Dread Names Red List for V20 with me. Outside of OPP she developed the Firefly RPG for Margaret Weis Productions, has written for Unknown Armies, All Flesh Must Be Eaten, Mistborn, Alethea, and Eclipse Phase to name a few.<br /> <br /> MMM</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in another thread, this is excellent news. Mortal Remains is one of my favorite OP books. It was well-written and had a ton of useful stuff. Doubtine Souls is great, and Dread Names Red List was also well done.<br /> <br /> I'm very pleased by this news.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:46:05-07:00","id":613646,"title":"","content":"I haven't really read through Mortal Remains and didn't give Doubting Souls as thorough a look as the other eras, but <i>holy crap</i> did I love the Firefly RPG. So this news has me happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:17:34-07:00","id":613696,"title":"","content":"Unknown Armies in my nWoD?<br /> <br /> Oh, happy day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:17:08-07:00","id":613768,"title":"","content":"I'm very happy to have Monica developing Hunter 2e! Her work and that of the freelancers on <i>Mortal Remains </i>and <i>Doubting Souls </i>were really cool.<br /> <br /> I hope she shares some thoughts with us here on the forums soon, maybe just a little something to whet the appetite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:45:50-07:00","id":614200,"title":"","content":"Welcome back to Hunter Monica.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T01:37:41-07:00","id":614715,"title":"","content":"Wait, Slasher Chronicle?<br /> <br /> ...<i>oh hell yes.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Comm